{title: One Man Die For The People}
{subtitle: John 11:47–53}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] [F/A] | [Gm] [Gm7/F] | [Eb] | [F7sus4] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]chief priests met with the Pharisees
They [Dm]sat in council and asked with care
[Gm]What are we doing, they questioned [Gm7/F]deep
This [Eb]man performs many signs, they said
[Bb]If he keeps on like this, they feared
[Dm7]Everyone will believe in him
The [Gm]Romans will come to take away [F6]
[Eb]Both our place and our nation
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It is [Bb]better that [F/A]one man [Gm]die
For the [Eb]people than the whole nation [F]perish
One man [Bb]die for the peo[F/A]ple
[Gm]Save us from the [Eb]end of [Bb]days [F/A][Gm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]One of them named Caiaphas spoke
He was [Dm7]high priest that very year
[Gm]You know nothing at all, he [Gm7/F]said
You [Eb]do not realize the truth
It is [Bb]better that [F/A]one man [Gm]die
For the [Eb]people than the whole nation [F]perish
He did not [Bb]say this on his [F/A]own
But being [Gm]high priest he [Eb]prophesied
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It is [Bb]better that [F/A]one man [Gm]die
For the [Eb]people than the whole nation [F]perish
One man [Bb]die for the peo[F/A]ple
[Gm]Save us from the [Eb]end of days
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Jesus [Eb]was going to die for the nation
And not [Bb]for the nation [Eb]only
But to gather into one
The [Cm7]scattered children of God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
It [Eb]is better that one man die
For the [Bb]people than [F/A]the whole na[Gm]tion perish
[Eb]One man die for the people
[F]Save us from the end [Bb]of days
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
From that [F/A]day on [Gm]they plotted
To [Eb]put him to [Bb]death
{end_of_verse}

